# The control layer: the files whose change buys a paid review at the landing (cc-land, gate_tier). Everything
# else lands on the gates it reaches and the planning session's own read of the diff (owner, 2026-09-04).
# One path or glob per line, relative to the tree this file describes (bin/…, not core/bin/…). Read from the
# BASE side of a diff, so a PR cannot take itself off this list.
#
# What belongs here: anything that runs unattended (a unit, a timer, a hook), or touches secrets, GitHub, pushes,
# permissions, the sandbox, the model switch, alerting, or the landing itself. What does not: a report or display
# tool, the board, wording, prose.

# the landing, and what it starts
bin/cc-land
bin/cc-loop
bin/cc
bin/cc-checkpoint
bin/cc-handoff
bin/cc-context
bin/cc-sandbox
bin/ccbox
ccbox/*

# the commit gate: runs unattended on every commit, and every static check this repo has hangs off it
.githooks/*

# secrets, GitHub, pushes, permissions
bin/cc-gh-token
bin/cc-publish
bin/cc-config
bin/cc-settings
bin/cc-trust
bin/cc-guard
bin/cc-scope
bin/cc-units
install.sh

# the model switch, and what pays for a model
bin/cc-limit
bin/cc-model
bin/cc-secretary
bin/cc-audit
bin/cc-spend
bin/cc-owed
bin/cc-evals

# alerting, and what reaches the owner or a session unasked
bin/cc-slack
bin/cc-notify
bin/cc-digest
bin/cc-msg
bin/cc-broker
bin/cc-pulse

# the rest of what runs unattended
bin/cc-reconcile
bin/cc-janitor
bin/cc-pause
bin/cc-vitals
bin/cc-heartbeat
bin/cc-boot
bin/cc-boot-notify
bin/cc-rc

# what becomes live configuration
config/*
templates/*
slack/*
